{
 "uid": "utm-obs-01-health",
 "title": "01 - Platform Health",
 "description": "**Purpose:** the primary operational dashboard. Answers *what is failing and where* for Kubernetes workloads across all utm-* namespaces.\n\n**Data sources:** Prometheus / kube-state-metrics.\n\n**Interpretation:** the Restart Leaderboard reports the cumulative counter AND the 1h rate. A high total with a zero rate is historical damage that has since stabilised; a non-zero rate is an active crash loop.\n\n**Drill-down:** Namespace Health → *02 - Kubernetes Workloads* → *03 - Nodes* → *04 - Ceph*.\n\n**Limitation:** container-level failure reasons are available, but application logs are NOT (no log shipper). See *08 - Observability Coverage*.",
 "tags": [
  "utm-observability",
  "health"
 ],
 "timezone": "browser",
 "editable": true,
 "graphTooltip": 1,
 "schemaVersion": 41,
 "version": 0,
